WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.360
Father Aksel. Neurotic.

2
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.880
Wanted to become a great musician,
but is an ordinary violin teacher.

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.880
In principle extremely embarrassing person.

4
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.600
Mother Laura. Also neurotic.

5
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.920
But she pays for everything
and can demand all kind of crap.

6
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.960
She pays for everything
in return of nothing.

7
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.480
Then me. Mihkel. The heir.
Carrier of bloodline and name.

8
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.920
Kind of family logo.

9
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.480
Sister Ave.
Incarnation of evil.

10
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.680
What are you doing?
Perve.

11
00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.520
Stop it. Stop it!

12
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.800
Can’t understand,
why it took so long.

13
00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.960
It’s a simple word – divorce.

14
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.720
I would like to…
- I want to…

15
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.320
Yes?

16
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.480
I think…
- I think…

17
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.280
I think…
- In my…

18
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:49.640
I wanted to say there’s no sense
in this marriage counselling.

19
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.720
We’re here because of our friends,
they still believe… in something.

20
00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.360
Well, they’re worried for your parents,

21
00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.440
hardworking ordinary people,
who believe in tradition.

22
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.760
Daughter’s divorce
is a public humiliation for them.

23
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.840
Thank you.
- You’re welcome.

24
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.360
Right. Let’s take it easy.

25
00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.560
Without any obligations,
without parents, children,

26
00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.520
without this
what-the-others-will-think rubbish.

27
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.240
Do you agree?

28
00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.880
Two ordinary people –
Laura and Aksel.

29
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.480
Just tell me, what is going on?

30
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.320
DIVORCE IN PEACE

31
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.040
Is porridge ready?
- Any minute.

32
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.160
No more regular milk?

33
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.720
Buckwheat milk?

34
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:41.120
It’ll scramble in coffee.
Coffee will taste like cat’s vomit.

35
00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:44.400
You don’t drink milk.
- I’m talking about coffee.

36
00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.680
I don’t drink coffee.

37
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.960
Indeed.
Why can’t you buy regular milk?

38
00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.600
Lactose free milk.
Is somebody lactose intolerant?

39
00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.840
Are you listening to me?
- What?

40
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.280
What did I just say?
- Don’t know. Cat’s vomit?

41
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.600
I’m asking is somebody
in the family lactose intolerant?

42
00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.640
No, it tastes better.
Ave is vegan.

43
00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.080
Vegan.

44
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.080
Soon there’ll be no regular food
in the house.

45
00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.040
Are we living in space station?

46
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.200
Meat in marmalade tubes
and potatoes in the form of pills.

47
00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:37.880
If you want regular food,
then go and buy yourself.

48
00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.040
I can’t see the point.

49
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.440
You are working in town,
I’m working at home.

50
00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.400
Why should we buy double groceries.

51
00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.440
Look, I’m…

52
00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:51.600
Never mind.

53
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.560
Disgusting, simply disgusting.

54
00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.480
I’m drinking black coffee.
For your information.

55
00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.040
Poured the wheat coffee down the sink.

56
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.440
Plumbing doesn’t have to tolerate
lactose or whatever… protein.

57
00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.280
Went really easily down the sink.
The buckwheat slime.

58
00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.440
Then all is well.

59
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.440
Children protesting in streets
against global warming.

60
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.560
My god, where are their parents?
Why are they not in school?

61
00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.760
It’s an important topic?
Children will have to live in this world.

62
00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.920
Right. And the white middle-aged man
is blamed for everything.

63
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.960
We are farting together with cows
creating holes in ozone layer.

64
00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.440
I simply said children are smarter
and more grown-up than we think.

65
00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.840
Simply childish!
Here’s permissive parenting for you.

66
00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.200
The world becomes infantile.

67
00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:18.600
We do what we want, run around
in streets, speak nonsense.

68
00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:22.840
We’ll protest and think of learning math
when loan advisor takes our house away.

69
00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.360
All right.

70
00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:29.960
All right. Nothing else to say.
Nothing to argue over, all is clear.

71
00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.480
I want a divorce.

72
00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.000
Did you hear what I said?
- What?

73
00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.480
Did you hear what I just said?

74
00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.080
You? About children,
wanting to live.

75
00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.840
I want a divorce.
- A divorce?

76
00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.400
I want a divorce.

77
00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:51.560
- Because of climate warming?
Because of us.

78
00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.760
What are you talking about?
- I’m serious.

79
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.120
Aksel, I don’t want
to live with you any longer.

80
00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.520
Laura, wait.
- No, I wouldn’t wait.

81
00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.760
I have given it serious thought.
It will happen now.

82
00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:04.120
I really don’t want this
buckwheat milk.

83
00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:07.640
It’s not about milk or climate,
it’s about us.

84
00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.640
Wait a little, Laura …
- No! I have been waiting for 25 years.

85
00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.600
Continue. Be brave…

86
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.920
I have given consideration to this
for a long time.

87
00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.120
I have said it out loud now.

88
00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:39.160
Tell me,
has somebody told you rubbish?

89
00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.960
What? No.

90
00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.120
Are you seeing somebody else?
- No, I’m not.

91
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.080
No? Then I can’t understand.

92
00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:49.560
Do I really have to explain?
Can’t you see it yourself?

93
00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.160
What?
- Of course not...

94
00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.160
You have your violin lessons
and whining. You see nothing.

95
00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.720
What? What should I see?

96
00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:02.480
Nothing has been functioning for years.
Nothing is functioning for us.

97
00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.560
Okay.

98
00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.280
But it’s functioning for me.

99
00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.720
Marriage is not an optical illusion,
which works for one person only.

100
00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.800
It has to work for both.

101
00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.240
See, you are becoming hysterical.

102
00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.120
Me? I’m not hysterical.
- Yes you are.

103
00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.440
I’m not.
– You are hysterical!

104
00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.200
You are hysterical!
- No, you are!

105
00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.760
Look at yourself! Maybe I have been …
sometimes… a few details you don’t like.

106
00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:30.360
What details? You say details.
You are talking about our life.

107
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.400
These details mount up into a big pile.

108
00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.080
Today is Tauno’s birthday party…
What should we do?

109
00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.520
What about it?
- Should we go there?

110
00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.800
We are going there.
- Are we? Separately?

111
00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.880
No, together.
- Together?

112
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.640
Everything, all the procedures…
This will take time.

113
00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:47.040
You are not thinking adequately.

114
00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.880
Yes, I am.
- You are not!

115
00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.080
What will you tell your parents?
- Exactly how things are.

116
00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.800
Exactly how things are...!

117
00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.800
Tell me what is really going on?

118
00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.600
What about children?
What will happen to them?

119
00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:06.640
Children are grown-up.
Children are at right age for divorce.

120
00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.120
Okay, I have to go to work.

121
00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.080
Right. She has to go to work.
Of course!

122
00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.720
Go to work and leave me here
with all this knowledge.

123
00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:18.960
We’ll continue in the evening.
- Of course...

124
00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:22.440
And don’t you worry.
I’ll bring a present for Tauno.

125
00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.560
And I’ll bring flowers
and something for Mirjam.

126
00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:29.160
Sure. The main thing the present.
A gift from heaven!

127
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.080
Elle!

128
00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.960
Elle…
I’m… sorry for acting like that.

129
00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.720
I wanted to clear one thing with you…
- What do you want?

130
00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.560
I wanted to ask have you told anybody

131
00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.360
what happened between us
at music school’s Christmas party?

132
00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:55.840
That sudden…
unplanned… improvised…

133
00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.040
There’s nothing to speak about.

134
00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:03.840
Right. I just thought that…
- I have told nobody.

135
00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:08.280
Then nobody knows about it?
- No.

136
00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:12.800
Elle, I thought about calling you
and to ask how you are…

137
00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.240
Why?

138
00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:18.760
Well, would have been respectable
after what had happened between us…

139
00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.080
What do you think happened?

140
00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.440
Stevie Wonder was singing,
we were dancing.

141
00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:28.120
You forced me behind the fridge.
We kissed, you had an orgasm and left.

142
00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.680
I see, that’s what I’m talking about…
Somebody might have seen us, Elle.

143
00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:34.320
Nobody saw because nothing happened.

144
00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.880
Elle, I wanted to call you.

145
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.760
There’s no need to worry.
Good-bye.

146
00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.840
Let’s agree we will tell nothing
to Tauno and Mirjam.

147
00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.520
Thank you for that. No need to
traumatize the man on his birthday.

148
00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:28.440
Do I look all right?
- Yes.

149
00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.480
Come on in!
- Happy birthday, Tauno!

150
00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.320
Happy birthday!

151
00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.600
Only the best are present.

152
00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.200
Tauno already celebrated
with his forest brothers.

153
00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.400
With Defence League men and hunters.

154
00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.560
Grunted for two days afterwards
like a wild boar.

155
00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.440
Enough, enough.

156
00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.840
Time to open presents!

157
00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:15.960
Oh, oh, oh.
Get lost! No way… What?

158
00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.880
Wait, there’s something more.

159
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.280
Go away! Oh boy!

160
00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:33.640
What? My taste exactly.

161
00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:37.640
You can wear these pants
to rumble around with forest brothers.

162
00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.440
Defence League men.
Should I put these on?

163
00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:46.160
You chose, right?
Of course will wear these. Hop!

164
00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:51.160
Let’s do the other way round.

165
00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.080
Happy birthday!

166
00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:12.240
My old man is a year older again.

167
00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.960
Laura, look.
I gave myself also a small present.

168
00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.520
Really cute.

169
00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.320
Ladies’ choice.

170
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:38.600
There. Look, my new sweetie.

171
00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.880
Nice instrument.
How many you already have?

172
00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.840
This is fifth. Look!
Do you feel?

173
00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:47.080
Rather heavy.

174
00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.960
Are you nuts?
Even an empty barrel can fire a shot!

175
00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:56.160
Sorry. I usually check this way
is violin straight.

176
00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:00.680
Violin!
Hey, have you heard this?

177
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:06.200
Bear and rabbit found a gun
in the forest. Studied it closer.

178
00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.320
Bear puts barrel into his mouth,
rabbit fiddles at gun’s butt plate.

179
00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:15.160
Suddenly Bang!
Bear’s lower jaw is blown away.

180
00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:19.360
Rabbit says... "What are you grinning at!
I’m already bloody frightened!"

181
00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.280
If you want
I can give the old set to you.

182
00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.440
I don’t know…

183
00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:43.040
What’s wrong?

184
00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:46.200
We don’t need any more.

185
00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.560
What do you mean by that?
Has something happened?

186
00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.720
Mirjam, promise me
you wouldn’t tell Tauno.

187
00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:02.040
Wow! Of course I wouldn’t.
What’s going on?

188
00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.680
We are getting divorced.

189
00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.440
But you can’t tell Tauno,
I promised to Aksel.

190
00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.680
You are getting divorced? You?

191
00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:15.880
Well, me and Laura. I found out today
and didn’t want to tell you yet.

192
00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:23.960
Maybe it’s only a passing whim,
but Laura is so sure, so decisive.

193
00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:29.320
What nonsense it this?
Here things are done differently.

194
00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:33.360
I will sort this out.
I will not allow you to divorce.

195
00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:37.320
I will sort this out.
- But how?

196
00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:41.280
It doesn’t function any longer.

197
00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:43.880
But you have no problems!

198
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:48.080
Well, we do. We are apart
for quite a long time already.

199
00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:50.080
Jesus, Aksel!

200
00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.520
Ok. Ok. I do understand.
Sometimes we too, with Tauno…

201
00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.400
Yes, people do fight.

202
00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:00.120
It’s not a whim,
not even a fight.

203
00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:04.160
But you have children.
- You can’t do this to Mikk and Ave.

204
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.200
I do understand
it’s complicated for you,

205
00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:08.640
because you don’t…
they don’t come to…

206
00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.520
You can speak it out,
Tauno can’t have children.

207
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:16.160
True,
but I’m processing the idea to adopt.

208
00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.800
See, we have problems, but you?

209
00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.200
Mihkel and Ave are grown-up.

210
00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:25.080
And you can’t live together
for the sake of children, can you?

211
00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:26.840
I don’t know.

212
00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:31.160
See… Congratulations
on the beginning of new life!

213
00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.200
It’s about money, right?
We can help you.

214
00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:36.600
No, no, no.

215
00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.600
It’s only about us.
It’s about nothing else.

216
00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:44.440
But you are not even fighting.
- Yes, we are not even fighting.

217
00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:48.280
You can’t demolish
what you have built together.

218
00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.920
Together? What have we built together?

219
00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:54.760
I built the house. He was
fingering the bow and… Forget it...

220
00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.320
It’s about the violin?
Let’s smash it!

221
00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:00.640
No. It’s not about violin.
It’s about us. Only about us.

222
00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:04.040
Aksel, what have you done?
You have cheated on Laura, right?

223
00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.440
No, I haven’t.

224
00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.840
I simply can’t understand.
Are you violent?

225
00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:12.640
No. Good god, no!
- Sorry, I simply can’t understand!

226
00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:18.120
I’m not violent.
Laura thinks we have grown apart.

227
00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.440
You are like two peas in a pod.

228
00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:23.160
Turns out we are not two peas in a pod.

229
00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:26.160
We are more like a pea and a bean.
Tomato and cabbage.

230
00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.400
You can’t do that so easily.

231
00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.240
It wouldn’t be easy for sure.
It wouldn’t be easy for her.

232
00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.160
I’m sure of that.

233
00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.400
Are you… are you separating?

234
00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:39.040
We’ll sell the house, divide property.
The way these things are done.

235
00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.560
Who will move into your house?
- This remains a very deep dark secret.

236
00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.440
Aksel, Laura.

237
00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:53.800
If you’ll need something,
we will be here.

238
00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:59.200
Want to speak. Everything is allowed.
No need to feel shame. All is allowed.

239
00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:06.000
Tears are allowed. Manly spring water.
We can’t lose you.

240
00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.560
I wish...

241
00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:15.920
...for a new optical sight.

242
00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.200
Tauno!

243
00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:23.000
Right. Divorce.
Let’s talk about divorce.

244
00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.200
Well, I though your job was
to talk Laura round.

245
00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:29.800
I’m a relationship coach,
not a lawyer.

246
00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:33.040
My aim is to keep you
in this new relationship

247
00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:36.120
as sound as possible.
- In new relationship?

248
00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:39.960
Divorce is a form of relationship.

249
00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:45.480
It’s very important that both parties
are not permanently damaged.

250
00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.120
You can’t yank the arrow
from one’s heart.

251
00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:52.160
You have to control the process.
- I don’t…

252
00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:55.840
You don’t want to divorce
like some neurotic East Europeans?

253
00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:59.000
You want to divorce gracefully
like Nordic people

254
00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:01.440
and at the same time, to remain intact.

255
00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:04.560
I don’t want to divorce at all.
- Listen!

256
00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:07.640
You can divorce sensibly and safely.

257
00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:15.240
I have a special 10-step programme.
“10 Steps to a Happy Divorce.”

258
00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:20.000
Each card inside represents
one phase of your marriage,

259
00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.480
which you have to outgrow amicably.
- What the hell…

260
00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:29.280
First mission.
“Good-bye to your first hello.”

261
00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:35.960
Revive your very first meeting
and say farewell to the memory.

262
00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:46.240
We have to face children together
and make the announcement.

263
00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:50.040
I wouldn’t rush with this
unless we are sure about the divorce.

264
00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.040
We are very sure about this.
- I see.

265
00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:57.240
What about your parents?
- I will tell them. Myself.

266
00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:01.720
Let’s agree that you will not meddle in
until I have told my parents, right?

267
00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.440
Thank you.

268
00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:20.880
Well, I’ll go then
and sleep in the living room.

269
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:26.680
Where you have been sleeping lately.
Passing away in front of television.

270
00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:34.720
What about these stupid
therapy assignments?

271
00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:39.560
I think we should take them seriously.
- Right.

272
00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:43.720
So... Our first meeting.

273
00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:47.240
What was it like?
- You can’t remember?

274
00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:51.320
I do remember. It was at a party.
I saw you.

275
00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:56.080
I was studying in conservatory
and you in art school.

276
00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:59.200
You arrived with that cool guy.
Everybody was staring at him.

277
00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.120
Yes, Tõnu. Total looser.
- Really?

278
00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.800
Come on!
– Was he?

279
00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:09.240
Of course. He has gone away.
Somewhere in Austria. Disappeared.

280
00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.080
So he choose something else
instead of music?

281
00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.880
No, he’s a conductor.
In a small town.

282
00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:21.600
In some opera house.
Somewhere in Vienna …

283
00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:23.280
Okay.

284
00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:27.760
He was a bludger from the very start,
not a serious musician.

285
00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:29.480
Not like you?

286
00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:34.200
I would if I only didn’t …
have stage fright. It’s not my fault.

287
00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.480
I could have performed on great stages.

288
00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:41.600
So you’re like an ingenious painter
with brush allergy?

289
00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:49.280
How did we… this meeting.

290
00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:54.400
How did it happen?

291
00:21:54.520 --> 00:22:02.640
I was at this party. You were with him.
We began to talk.

292
00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:07.200
You were wearing school uniform.
Everybody was laughing at you.

293
00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.840
Laughing?
- Yes. You had school’s cap on.

294
00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:13.800
Right. I came straight from a concert.
- Well, okay.

295
00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:18.720
And then you stepped on my toe.

296
00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:26.400
Well, I’ll step on then.

297
00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:36.240
And then?

298
00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:39.960
You sputtered and explained something.

299
00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:44.400
I had just bet Juta that I will kiss
the first guy I’ll meet.

300
00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:47.400
I see, that was a surprise.

301
00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:50.800
Did we…?

302
00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:52.160
You don’t remember?

303
00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:55.280
Yes, I do remember. It was improper.

304
00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:57.080
I don’t think so.

305
00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:00.120
It was… shameless.
– Shameless?

306
00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:04.160
And it was shameless too
when you couldn’t leave me alone,

307
00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:07.520
followed me and climbed in
through my dorm’s window?

308
00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:11.200
Well, I was under influence,
under your influence.

309
00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:15.520
What could I do?

310
00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:20.760
You weren’t under my influence, Aksel.
You were alive!

311
00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:24.880
Yes, I was. These were strange times.

312
00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:31.720
Shit! It’s a strange game.
I don’t want to… I wouldn’t agree.

313
00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.920
I wouldn’t agree with the divorce.
Why should I agree with this therapy?

314
00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:39.480
You were told, there will be scars.
- Scars will be there anyway.

315
00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:43.720
Ok. I don’t bother either.
No need, it’s really lame. Absurd.

316
00:23:43.840 --> 00:23:47.480
No. As you threw down the gauntlet
with such an ease,

317
00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:51.320
you had to count
the challenge will be accepted.

318
00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:55.400
So, let’s do it.
How things were in your dormitory?

319
00:23:55.520 --> 00:23:58.880
I climbed in through the window.
Exactly!

320
00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.760
Not a big deal, let’s do it.
What the hell!

321
00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:09.960
Aksel, stop it. You’ll hurt yourself.
- I’m already hurt.

322
00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:13.760
Oh dear god!

323
00:24:17.600 --> 00:24:19.200
Aksel?

324
00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:21.160
Did you fall out of the window?

325
00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.160
Shit! Window sill was slippery.

326
00:24:34.680 --> 00:24:36.800
Have you already heard?
- Yes.

327
00:24:38.280 --> 00:24:41.760
Totally crazy.
A nervous breakdown?

328
00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:48.760
No, c’mon.
I’m worried about entrance exam.

329
00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:53.560
Your what-its-name film school?
- Yes, exactly the same school.

330
00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:55.880
Then get started.
Do something.

331
00:24:56.000 --> 00:25:01.760
Children…Mihkel, Ave.
We have something to tell you.

332
00:25:03.040 --> 00:25:05.040
Get divorced!

333
00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:13.360
That went rather well.

334
00:25:20.760 --> 00:25:23.560
Laura, wait!
- I have to go to work.

335
00:25:23.680 --> 00:25:27.520
I’ll understand, but let’s say
I will change whatever that means.

336
00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:30.880
In theory, I’ll admit,
where I have made mistakes.

337
00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:34.480
Could we go on?
- You will never change.

338
00:25:34.600 --> 00:25:36.840
Laura, are you so sure?
– Yes.

339
00:25:55.920 --> 00:25:57.760
That’s enough.

340
00:25:59.360 --> 00:26:01.320
For today.

341
00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:09.200
You are doing well, Roberta, very well.

342
00:26:09.320 --> 00:26:12.640
It’s about me. I’m under weather.

343
00:26:16.760 --> 00:26:19.320
Let’s practice longer on Wednesday.

344
00:26:19.440 --> 00:26:21.200
This is yours.

345
00:26:22.720 --> 00:26:24.360
Yes.

346
00:26:29.640 --> 00:26:32.840
She has made up her mind.
There’s nothing to do.

347
00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:38.280
Wait, listen to me.
First step - politeness.

348
00:26:38.400 --> 00:26:40.200
I am polite.

349
00:26:41.920 --> 00:26:45.720
Women like this sometimes,
when you’ll help them with the coat.

350
00:26:45.840 --> 00:26:48.840
Laura doesn’t like these things.
She’s a modern woman.

351
00:26:48.960 --> 00:26:52.600
Keeps up with modern ideas.
Equal opportunities and all that.

352
00:26:52.720 --> 00:26:58.560
Modern women don’t like masculine men.
Man has to be like a castrated walrus.

353
00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:01.320
Then women are content.

354
00:27:01.440 --> 00:27:05.440
Shit! Not even then.
They are never content. It's hopeless!

355
00:27:05.560 --> 00:27:12.000
You have to try. Politeness.
Second step. Exercise.

356
00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:15.240
You’ll go to a gym,
get yourself in good shape.

357
00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:20.480
Why should I become a breeding bull?
- Stand straight, chin up!

358
00:27:20.600 --> 00:27:27.000
That’s what was missing in our marriage...
- Standing straight helps always.

359
00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:30.480
Maybe not when approaching
a working helicopter.

360
00:27:30.600 --> 00:27:34.280
Third step.
You’ll pay me a visit once a day.

361
00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:37.320
I’ll give you a punchbag.
You’ll let the steam out,

362
00:27:37.440 --> 00:27:40.000
will be calm at home
and wouldn’t whine.

363
00:27:40.120 --> 00:27:42.360
And that’s that? Your recipe?

364
00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:46.320
The last serious step
comes in the end.

365
00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:51.080
“Tauno’s Staying Together in 5 steps.”

366
00:27:51.200 --> 00:27:58.080
Step 5. Take her to a theatre.

367
00:27:58.200 --> 00:28:03.800
It’s like hiding a carrot in straw.
Roe deers go crazy.

368
00:28:08.560 --> 00:28:10.600
I know what I have to do.

369
00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:15.280
We’ll need more dough. Yes.
The whole wedding table.

370
00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:18.560
All the desserts will come
from our shop. I told.

371
00:28:23.120 --> 00:28:26.680
In brief. I thought
this divorce was end of torture.

372
00:28:27.440 --> 00:28:29.840
Actually, this was just the beginning.

373
00:28:37.960 --> 00:28:40.400
Mother, father. Hello.

374
00:28:42.280 --> 00:28:46.440
What is going on?
Laura, you are getting divorced?

375
00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:49.160
Dear daughter, is this true?

376
00:28:50.160 --> 00:28:51.680
Aksel...

377
00:28:53.920 --> 00:28:55.600
Mihkel?
